  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added an ordinary CPython-parseable, representation-neutral protocol for canonical row and column generator matrices. It computes one canonical echelon result, asks a domain adapter for its actual leading generator-row count, bulk-selects those rows, validates structural dimensions with the exact __index__ protocol, marks the result immutable through an explicit callback, and returns already-echelonized metadata for the future subspace adapter. This distinction is essential for composite Zmod(n): a Howell form can have more nonzero canonical generator rows than its algebraic rank or even the source matrix row count. Wide and tall Zmod(6) regressions compare the Sage.js Howell matrices with explicit bidirectional generator changes certified by SageMath. Cross-ring row_space(base_ring=...) remains a separate noncanonical GeneratorSpan. CPython call-count tests and Sage.js differentials also cover ZZ HNF, QQ/GF(7)/GF(2) field bases, rank zero, degenerate shapes, exact canonical forms, immutability, and base-ring planning. Warm 200x300 extraction remains materially faster than scalar reconstruction across every covered domain.",
    "risks": [
      "This lane deliberately does not modify public matrix.py, so Matrix.row_space() and Matrix.column_space() still use the scalar-decoding implementation until the integration lane wires this protocol.",
      "The shared test/node-test-manifest.cjs and pyrightconfig.json were not claimed because another active lane owns the manifest and the task was scoped to new files. Focused Pyright passed, but integration must register both the test and module before the global runner can accept the new files.",
      "Cross-ring GeneratorSpan records Sage's required already_echelonized=False path, but the eventual public subspace constructor must implement that ring-aware generator canonicalization; it cannot use the same fast echelon basis as the equal-ring case."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Register test/linear-matrix-subspaces.cjs in the unit tier and add src/lib/sagejs/linear_algebra/matrix_subspaces.py to pyrightconfig.json during integration.",
      "Wire Matrix.row_space(), row_module(), image(), column_space(), and column_module() through the new canonical-basis protocol once public matrix.py is no longer under an overlapping selection lane.",
      "Teach VectorSubspaceParent or its constructor adapter to consume already_echelonized and immutable metadata without canonicalizing the selected generator matrix again, and implement the GeneratorSpan fallback for a distinct row-space base ring.",
      "Give the public Zmod(n) adapter a packed leading-nonzero-row count for Howell forms; rank is only a valid basis-row-count callback over ZZ and fields.",
      "Run the full native/integration suite after shared registrations and public wiring; this representation-neutral lane itself adds no native boundary."
    ]
  }
}
